uthor": {"login": "SylvainBoilard", "id": 1705540, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDU1NDA=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1705540?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard", "html_url": "https://github.com/SylvainBoilard", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "committer": {"login": "SylvainBoilard", "id": 1705540, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDU1NDA=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1705540?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard", "html_url": "https://github.com/SylvainBoilard", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/SylvainBoilard/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "parents": [{"sha": "49c3ff00c7cf462380b7c42e8de0412e2a2372d3", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ocaml/opam-repository/commits/49c3ff00c7cf462380b7c42e8de0412e2a2372d3", "html_url": "https://github.com/ocaml/opam-repository/commit/49c3ff00c7cf462380b7c42e8de0412e2a2372d3"}]}, {"sha": "bac9c3858cff51b3d7c9a6f6990799bbe7582c01", "node_id": "C_kwDOAETL7doAKGJhYzljMzg1OGNmZjUxYjNkN2M5YTZmNjk5MDc5OWJiZTc1ODJjMDE", "commit": {"author": {"name": "Sylvain Boilard", "email": "boilard@crans.org", "date": "2026-11-17T20:02:38Z"}, "committer": {"name": "Sylvain Boilard", "email": "boilard@crans.org", "date": "2026-11-17T23:57:25Z"}, "message": "Package glfw-ocaml (3.4 and 3.5)\n\nCHANGES (3.4):\n\n* Added\n\n- Support for the new GLFW 3.4 features, including the new exceptions (`CursorUnavailable`, `FeatureUnavailable`, `FeatureUnimplemented`, `PlatformUnavailable`), the new init hints (`Platform`, `AnglePlatformType`, `X11XcbVulkanSurface`, `WaylandLibdecor`), the new window hints and attributes (e.g. `MousePassthrough`, `PositionX` and `PositionY`, `ScaleFramebuffer`, `Win32KeyboardMenu`, `Win32ShowDefault`, `WaylandAppID`), the new cursor shapes and the `Captured` cursor mode, named gamepad buttons and axes (`gamepad_button_*`, `gamepad_axis_*`) and the new functions `getPlatform`, `platformSupported` and `getWindowTitle`.\n\n* Changed\n\n- Flag lists (key modifiers, joystick hats) are now returned in ascending order.\n- `getGamepadState` now raises `InvalidValue` when the joystick is not connected or is not a gamepad, instead of returning meaningless data.\n- `getPrimaryMonitor` now raises `Failure` when there is no primary monitor.\n- `getKey` and `getKeyScancode` now raise `Invalid_argument` when called with `Unknown`.\n- `Image.create` now requires strictly positive dimensions.\n- The compatibility of the installed GLFW package version is now checked with pkg-config at build time.\n\n* Fixed\n\n- The window attributes `DoubleBuffer`, `ContextDebug`, `ContextNoError` and `ContextReleaseBehavior` can now be read with `getWindowAttrib`.\n- The missing key modifiers `CapsLock` and `NumLock` have been added.\n- The joystick callback now reports `Connected` and `Disconnected` correctly.\n- `getWindowAttrib` no longer fails on the `ContextReleaseBehavior` attribute.\n- The dimension check in `Image.create` can no longer overflow.\n- `getClipboardString` no longer crashes when GLFW returns `NULL`.\n- Joysticks with many buttons or hats are now handled correctly.\n- Memory allocation failures now raise `OutOfMemory` instead of crashing.\n- An exception raised inside a callback is now reported as a fatal uncaught exception instead of escaping into C code.\n- Calling `terminate` without having destroyed every window first no longer leaks memory.\n- The error callback no longer risks using an invalidated value if a garbage collection happens at the wrong time.\n\n* Requirements\n\n- OCaml >= 4.03.0\n- dune >= 3.1\n\n* Known limitations\n\n- `getPrimaryMonitor` and `getGamepadState` raise exceptions instead of returning an option type; this will be fixed in the next major version (see the README).\n\n---\n\nCHANGES (3.5):\n\n* Added\n\n- Support for the new GLFW 3.5 feature, the `UnlimitedMouseButtons` input mode.", "tree": {"sha": "7169158e07a009edc26b8e20fe613aff47f43996", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ocaml/opam-repository/git/trees/7169158e07a009edc26b8e20fe613aff47f43996"}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ocaml/opam-repository/git/commits/bac9c3858cff51b3d7c9a6f6990799bbe7582c01", "comment_count": 0, "verification": {"verified": false, "reason": "unsigned", "signature": null, "payload": null, "verified_at": null}}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ocaml/opam-repository/commits/bac9c3858cff51b3d7c9a6f6990799bbe7582c01", "html_url": "https://github.com/ocaml/opam-repository/commit/bac9c3858cff51b3d7c9a6f6990799bbe7582c